   "id": 535644,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Many species of pine trees are found in different geographical locations in North America and Canada. This is because _____.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1048872,
     "content_html": "they were not separated geographically over millions of years and did not evolve to be different species."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048873,
     "content_html": "plant breeders carried seeds to different areas."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048874,
     "content_html": "pollen from pollen tree was able to travel far."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048875,
     "content_html": "pine was present widely and in some areas they dried out."
    }
   ],
